[{:db/id "q-73551/selection/27dfd7b2f3a44fa4f4cc5761207dc531ddacca5029a04a4a9f6cb5cf30146e4e" :answer/id #uuid "442589b9-68c9-5dff-8707-51d36b03745a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73551/selection/0b9553a5d90a3a6951a3ad26f4f1a241a020197281464454f8e19e5e3e79def0" :answer/id #uuid "8baefa8d-9c50-50bb-ac7b-6e9b6dace74f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73551/selection/c5f67bf600896754ffd945a9559a82bcdce5e15c85493bc8b664d848215aa843" :answer/id #uuid "2475e2de-4a6b-54f8-be14-6625a724d4bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73551/selection/4875eb21adab58d53ffc49def12d54090b4361d9b742795c4275871d3a18e12f" :answer/id #uuid "f8a00f56-77fd-508c-a533-b5085fc148f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73551/selection/e0942a398863506991fecad8f153da6b84ef6349c4224b9a6196c827aceadc20" :answer/id #uuid "9fc59cb3-cdb5-560b-9621-68e5ee5291f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73551/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18651f35-a486-51f6-a80d-35e8c6ee7bf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73551/selection/27dfd7b2f3a44fa4f4cc5761207dc531ddacca5029a04a4a9f6cb5cf30146e4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-73551/selection/27dfd7b2f3a44fa4f4cc5761207dc531ddacca5029a04a4a9f6cb5cf30146e4e" "q-73551/selection/0b9553a5d90a3a6951a3ad26f4f1a241a020197281464454f8e19e5e3e79def0" "q-73551/selection/c5f67bf600896754ffd945a9559a82bcdce5e15c85493bc8b664d848215aa843" "q-73551/selection/4875eb21adab58d53ffc49def12d54090b4361d9b742795c4275871d3a18e12f" "q-73551/selection/e0942a398863506991fecad8f153da6b84ef6349c4224b9a6196c827aceadc20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73551" :question/id #uuid "08ec22c2-8cd9-5dca-af3f-944499fe851c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73551" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 5x-15y=10 \\\\  & 2x-4y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -15 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73551/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186257805 :question/answer-fields 17592186274432] {:db/id "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/8c1cd08d683f2a93d86f6038468cfd1e0443e87f82d50727a15a1c467ef5f413" :answer/id #uuid "6ccb3362-16ba-5f9e-9f8d-7e25092191a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/7bffa0a31fe7bbce70c9eaedc1eb7b5e251efaa8eed21c883dcfddf0aa4f19f0" :answer/id #uuid "16a00814-086e-5ba2-8237-c14372dd487f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/939d4701c3d666d8388d5644f43f87804fc355251f19bb70098480569581b025" :answer/id #uuid "4e32b6ea-cee4-5c0e-b6ea-d66eaabe37d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/1681c23ccb47be8f7d4b8966bcccbfd5944efebcf511e7d06bf9d06cf222fe8e" :answer/id #uuid "23533c7a-1ecd-5ed9-b5a4-5ff274b68e94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/ed05bd30d2fede7c37552e6e3489a630a294ade364cb7dd2caf877647979f4a8" :answer/id #uuid "7fba27ab-370f-5485-b428-c24daa7ddf13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "80a79e8b-afcf-52b4-9d47-b89d38c83f9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/7bffa0a31fe7bbce70c9eaedc1eb7b5e251efaa8eed21c883dcfddf0aa4f19f0" :answer-field/choices ["q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/8c1cd08d683f2a93d86f6038468cfd1e0443e87f82d50727a15a1c467ef5f413" "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/7bffa0a31fe7bbce70c9eaedc1eb7b5e251efaa8eed21c883dcfddf0aa4f19f0" "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/939d4701c3d666d8388d5644f43f87804fc355251f19bb70098480569581b025" "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/1681c23ccb47be8f7d4b8966bcccbfd5944efebcf511e7d06bf9d06cf222fe8e" "q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b/ed05bd30d2fede7c37552e6e3489a630a294ade364cb7dd2caf877647979f4a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-12669"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/assets/e92694d3fc8d6be220fc4d45c0d210a53076db72daad477c3199ece5c4460627.png)\n\nIdentify the equation that generated the graph above." :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/assets/51bf87385bc52632a0bf722d5672047e79afc8ea0556dabda3257c9ebd1e91a3.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, reflect it in the $x$-axis to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, translate it by $3$ units **down** to give $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3$\n\nTherefore, the given curve is the graph of $y=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3.$" :question/answer-fields ["q-12669/selection/ma-v1/05731bc845093de9e36a28140c539a76db0629de4a2158972979d99206c54f9b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" :answer/id #uuid "4d72ea02-ff80-58ef-aba1-1d9f83a6160b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825/selection/634196fc9bb48033d39ff9813af63434068332cb8c836d13c5213b0cd4323e90" :answer/id #uuid "549f9742-aeb3-5082-9612-6ec6bd2c2e26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825/selection/b46a89106abfbaaddd7e7797028c9f978d583e364a9adc93b2bb761d1ed0e4b9" :answer/id #uuid "fd993e3f-4d58-5847-a76d-6919cbadf320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825/selection/0eef758186e17eb7a5ee456810146e51542b13106810829634d974baad29ace4" :answer/id #uuid "8af61602-e5f1-50b0-b7fb-da21cf2dc2dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825/selection/ea49528aa95b43e5c15771869420f333ea70666c30a5af4d66e208543b968cbc" :answer/id #uuid "a11e5dfd-52e6-5b6d-9f2a-820bc2d1db43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c59e863d-947d-5701-b687-a25fe7f0fee9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75825/selection/ea49528aa95b43e5c15771869420f333ea70666c30a5af4d66e208543b968cbc" :answer-field/choices ["q-75825/selection/f3dac89f2ee5e33877fb0ae412fdefdc0cdcceb7dcdcd6e702e1e3ff0391e011" "q-75825/selection/634196fc9bb48033d39ff9813af63434068332cb8c836d13c5213b0cd4323e90" "q-75825/selection/b46a89106abfbaaddd7e7797028c9f978d583e364a9adc93b2bb761d1ed0e4b9" "q-75825/selection/0eef758186e17eb7a5ee456810146e51542b13106810829634d974baad29ace4" "q-75825/selection/ea49528aa95b43e5c15771869420f333ea70666c30a5af4d66e208543b968cbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75825" :question/id #uuid "2eba1a60-af4c-5293-b4c6-5aa086d9d5e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-75825" :question/problem "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-8=(x+2)(x-4).\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8} & =\\frac{3x-6}{(x+2)(x-4)}=\\frac{A}{x+2}+\\frac{B}{x-4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n3x-6=A(x-4)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=4,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(4)-6 & =A(4-4)+B(4+2) \\\\ 6 & =6B \\\\ B & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-2)-6 & =A(-2-4)+B(-2+2) \\\\ -12 & =-6A \\\\ A & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}=\\frac{2}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{x-4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{x-4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{x-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-4|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}(x-4)|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\frac{3x-6}{{x}^{2}-2x-8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}(x-4)|{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({5}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75825/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75825"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002/selection/b1aa6731c1d4190745c9879fcc79bf6ed4e14b36bffa70a59e51bccc5de87472" :answer/id #uuid "4dfd6ea7-7721-5e82-a44d-fc96ae2288cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002/selection/fc5c63badd53dc2e7900852eef5c79699c526a5a605eb9e5573a105d65c4def8" :answer/id #uuid "b6ca2841-afe6-562d-8f20-3c723ec559a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+7x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002/selection/08346d8dfb500c049a5fb306e069531dae298b48db41e506836c4da18a4643ba" :answer/id #uuid "36ef69af-328b-57ad-86e9-e80cbabf5414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002/selection/361837070bea7bb113ba6a1b89c4f2e71d2626eacc8c20eb2e7355247bb5ca47" :answer/id #uuid "ce753a21-a61a-560c-8022-6ea8c4575f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{x}^{3}-{8}^{2}+5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002/selection/facb5090774ed2cc32c9429f8092ed42a41b9c9f4a95051250bfe10f272860f7" :answer/id #uuid "0a4390eb-a399-562b-8873-113adf5bbf4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+5x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "db477c7e-c55e-56e5-8367-52b4d4376380" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338002/selection/b1aa6731c1d4190745c9879fcc79bf6ed4e14b36bffa70a59e51bccc5de87472" :answer-field/choices ["q-338002/selection/b1aa6731c1d4190745c9879fcc79bf6ed4e14b36bffa70a59e51bccc5de87472" "q-338002/selection/fc5c63badd53dc2e7900852eef5c79699c526a5a605eb9e5573a105d65c4def8" "q-338002/selection/08346d8dfb500c049a5fb306e069531dae298b48db41e506836c4da18a4643ba" "q-338002/selection/361837070bea7bb113ba6a1b89c4f2e71d2626eacc8c20eb2e7355247bb5ca47" "q-338002/selection/facb5090774ed2cc32c9429f8092ed42a41b9c9f4a95051250bfe10f272860f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338002" :question/id #uuid "a5d43506-b1e4-5efc-8f0c-eab49facef43" :question/math-academy-id "q-338002" :question/problem "If $D(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+2y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+y,$ then $D({x}^{3}-x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=x,{f}_{2}=2y,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=1.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{3}-x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{3}-x) & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{3}-x)+2({x}^{3}-x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{3}-x)+({x}^{3}-x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{x}^{2}-1)+2({x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2}-1)+({x}^{3}-x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+2({x}^{3}-x)\\cdot (6x)+({x}^{3}-x) \\\\  & =x\\cdot 6+12x({x}^{3}-x)+({x}^{3}-x) \\\\  & =12{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+5x\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338002/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338002"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188/selection/dcd1c3cf3257b3074e1d8bca34938e8b22d4b3daf29da18b58c85ca9805ec64e" :answer/id #uuid "5016a6a4-e836-59fc-89ce-492d9f5fccd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(1+x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188/selection/38c1ded84340ece5868745e1c116cb152ac01508dc86e6268fd9643965ae8684" :answer/id #uuid "8cd61209-a069-5d06-8e7e-d62ce79bb311" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(1-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188/selection/f05e5fa816477c9e9f452af1bc016765104f29faebb1e3aec1f21a622c283d10" :answer/id #uuid "00f133cf-41aa-5f4c-b646-78be1ceefcb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188/selection/926e39b2169289d06081816da4c485ba422d9a00bc2bd26718be141a90f04d33" :answer/id #uuid "170fac6a-9a77-53cc-94c3-29312d5ce325" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(2-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188/selection/53479aded7f3cfffee8b2eeaf8e9427326ec77ce92660e5a7254ca7c3a05465a" :answer/id #uuid "2ae4ff5b-12e9-5ef4-9c2a-40694e967721" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "96c2df66-1c37-50bc-830b-512f48b2a629" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338188/selection/38c1ded84340ece5868745e1c116cb152ac01508dc86e6268fd9643965ae8684" :answer-field/choices ["q-338188/selection/dcd1c3cf3257b3074e1d8bca34938e8b22d4b3daf29da18b58c85ca9805ec64e" "q-338188/selection/38c1ded84340ece5868745e1c116cb152ac01508dc86e6268fd9643965ae8684" "q-338188/selection/f05e5fa816477c9e9f452af1bc016765104f29faebb1e3aec1f21a622c283d10" "q-338188/selection/926e39b2169289d06081816da4c485ba422d9a00bc2bd26718be141a90f04d33" "q-338188/selection/53479aded7f3cfffee8b2eeaf8e9427326ec77ce92660e5a7254ca7c3a05465a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338188" :question/id #uuid "bde726cb-a972-5ec5-b386-e82b271ce8fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-338188" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ then $D({e}^{x})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=y,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={e}^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{x})-x({e}^{x})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{x})-x{e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-x{e}^{2x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{x}-x{e}^{2x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(1-x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338188/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338188"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024/selection/5846909f174da1ed620d151ac05204e83972966f779efb8f143352f971a29779" :answer/id #uuid "0425b281-3f9b-5fbf-95cd-223abca89024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024/selection/e733dc6bf0b88b1c1b230e32a5cfd5a69828f772e015dc33bed1ec14c8bbe147" :answer/id #uuid "4a79ee32-e878-53b9-932d-5ba87e2271bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024/selection/2b89602cbe8182b410e9840c62b2c64f14aa9f4f3b34896bfe6d36a7a17b24d1" :answer/id #uuid "ff8e8364-c69d-5298-9ef6-d9d24ee7cef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024/selection/c8530b2891d9503fb6de9f0eb973be3fd49bf431b04889083e8f7ddb6861ad0f" :answer/id #uuid "ff195ea3-4342-5a7e-ab1b-5862f60d1702" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024/selection/18de0fe9daabcf66b8e3c296b6ab97fad111b0cd0aa8728ac12c1ec9b9aa47c4" :answer/id #uuid "ff27dc57-e368-5eed-bd0c-ec2c96ad0e37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7361dbca-3d56-533f-971e-e8e60313830e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95024/selection/c8530b2891d9503fb6de9f0eb973be3fd49bf431b04889083e8f7ddb6861ad0f" :answer-field/choices ["q-95024/selection/5846909f174da1ed620d151ac05204e83972966f779efb8f143352f971a29779" "q-95024/selection/e733dc6bf0b88b1c1b230e32a5cfd5a69828f772e015dc33bed1ec14c8bbe147" "q-95024/selection/2b89602cbe8182b410e9840c62b2c64f14aa9f4f3b34896bfe6d36a7a17b24d1" "q-95024/selection/c8530b2891d9503fb6de9f0eb973be3fd49bf431b04889083e8f7ddb6861ad0f" "q-95024/selection/18de0fe9daabcf66b8e3c296b6ab97fad111b0cd0aa8728ac12c1ec9b9aa47c4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95024" :question/id #uuid "a6e27650-4b1b-5548-99e3-f1ed5cca0feb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95024" :question/problem "The time that a particular laptop battery lasts is normally distributed with a mean of $32$ hours and a standard deviation of $4$ hours. What is the probability that a full charge lasts for $36$ hours or more? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.8159\\,$ | $\\,0.8186\\,$ | $\\,0.8212\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.8413\\,$ | $\\,0.8438\\,$ | $\\,0.8461\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.1\\,$ | $\\,0.8643\\,$ | $\\,0.8665\\,$ | $\\,0.8686\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the time the full charge lasts. Then we have $X∼N(32,{4}^{2}).$\n\nWe want to find $P(X\\ge 36).$ Thus, we convert $X$ to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 36) & =P(Z\\ge \\frac{36-32}{4}) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge 1) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le 1) \\\\  & =1-Φ(1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $z$-table, we see that\n\n$$\n1-Φ(1)=1-0.8413≈0.1587.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a full charge lasts $36$ hours or more is approximately $0.16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95024/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "179e0482-8d67-5e28-af2d-0d3aa7f0b770"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-114961"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14070857/assets/d624edaffd8c90de40041d419cf65bcf8f3af5d31c8d88d1123bd8f3d7555166.png)\n\nWhat is the length of the major axis of the ellipse given above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "61123339-a598-5584-b840-bbec5ca32992" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8" :answer/id #uuid "970ffbb5-fc4f-567c-b886-152e4869c4d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d01c4c5b-9211-596b-9e33-618f21135344" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ace4a8cf-9fbd-5aa5-863d-a0728cd59e19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "79e06126-6a37-524b-9992-03f3b52476b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c775489-34cc-59ef-b15a-1d3f078d4bc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11636/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-11636/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-11636/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8" "q-11636/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-11636/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-11636/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11636" :question/id #uuid "76d4aee6-756f-5379-be4d-2041f6296474" :question/math-academy-id "q-11636" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AC=CA={I}_{3}$\n- $AD=DA={I}_{3}$\n- $D={A}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AD=DA={I}_{3}.$ Computing $AD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AD & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 7 & -17\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false. As a result, $D\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11636/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11636"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186256714 :question/answer-fields 17592186274201] {:db/id "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" :answer/id #uuid "9e6e4a72-3c67-5420-a6fe-db2d025b1ac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/bf115f260f45452679ee73113d67f317a6559746deafc4709c25a926163c9554" :answer/id #uuid "491b26c6-c021-5c0e-afe4-897fd97ebb1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/7b1aae932335f11f346ed4eb0c9afd6a061d6be8a7cea31763a71dd6bce664f5" :answer/id #uuid "4e2fa978-e172-5314-a0ec-11566a6e60f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/390b4bb54d3dedd651860316ae155150bf28127c5b6cd863edcb2d740b0d656f" :answer/id #uuid "b97e8f6e-6ca2-5aa2-bbef-baa0d205f6e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/f4b96082b46f39ad3f91f662bbb703b1be822eae05491060010da1e9a3349408" :answer/id #uuid "22268241-4d05-54e4-b39b-bf60b6db304e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e" :answer-field/id #uuid "c94defa3-f22f-5dda-aef8-6e6a76f4184a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/7b1aae932335f11f346ed4eb0c9afd6a061d6be8a7cea31763a71dd6bce664f5" :answer-field/choices ["q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/bf115f260f45452679ee73113d67f317a6559746deafc4709c25a926163c9554" "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/7b1aae932335f11f346ed4eb0c9afd6a061d6be8a7cea31763a71dd6bce664f5" "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/390b4bb54d3dedd651860316ae155150bf28127c5b6cd863edcb2d740b0d656f" "q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e/f4b96082b46f39ad3f91f662bbb703b1be822eae05491060010da1e9a3349408"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-107499"] :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{6}{-1+\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $-1-\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{6}{-1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(-1-\\text{i})}{(-1+\\text{i})(-1-\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(-1-\\text{i})}{(-1)^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(-1-\\text{i})}{1+1} \\\\  & =3(-1-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-3-3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=-3-3\\text{i},$ the magnitude is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=-3$ and $y=-3$ are both negative, $z$ lies in the third quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-3}{-3}| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=3\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-107499/selection/ma-v1/e21ba1ba1d9a6cbe0ffc4cec859ed9091afba91d09ce43fdbb6c91fb8237750e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186257410 :question/answer-fields 17592186274367] {:db/id "q-120300/selection/ma-v1/9bccbb6f8d492a6b9c5c3e1cd0ee2297a14900562287e146964305ddcee4569e/5c230e3ef5bbee24a432f3235e0ba5ce464b10c78ad5e527a5d31fbd25c827d1" :answer/id #uuid "9ab6cfa9-1d12-5b2f-8290-0e79ac0648b